"id": "section-1",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2 id=\"service-scope\">Emergency electrician Perth: service scope</h2><ul><li>Accept urgent private electrical repair requests 24 hours a day, including nights and weekends.</li><li>Investigate affected circuits, safety switches, outlets and lighting within the agreed repair scope.</li><li>Confirm the initial assessment and any subsequent repair or replacement separately in the plan and quote.</li><li>No guaranteed arrival time, free emergency attendance or public network repair is implied. Solar, batteries, gas and appliance internal repairs remain separate specialist scopes.</li></ul><p>We confirm the property, installation and requested outcome before selecting the work. Fixed plumbing and electrical tasks are handled by the appropriate qualified trade; a coordinated visit does not make every task interchangeable. Current documentation relevant to the proposed work can be requested privately.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"electrical.html\">Perth electrical services</a></li><li><a href=\"power-faults-perth.html\">Partial power loss and fault finding</a></li><li><a href=\"safety-switch-tripping-perth.html\">A safety switch that will not reset</a></li><li><a href=\"power-points-perth.html\">Damaged or failed power points</a></li><li><a href=\"contact.html?service=emergency-electrician-perth.html\">Routine electrical enquiries</a></li><li><a href=\"service-areas.html\">Perth service regions</a></li></ul></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "section-2",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section expanded-scenarios\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2 id=\"service-scenarios\">Common situations and what to report</h2><div class=\"expanded-scenario\"><h3>Partial power loss while neighbours still have supply</h3><p>Tell us whether lights, outlets or both are affected and when the change occurred. A private circuit fault and a network interruption are different issues. Neighbours having power can help describe the pattern, but it does not identify the fault or establish safety.</p></div><div class=\"expanded-scenario\"><h3>A safety switch trips at night or an outlet smells burnt</h3><p>Do not repeatedly reset protection or keep using damaged equipment. Describe the warning signs from a safe location. For shock, tingling or network danger, contact Western Power first; an urgent repair call is not a replacement for emergency reporting.</p></div><p>These are illustrative situations, not customer case studies or diagnoses. Report what you have noticed; you do not need to identify the cause before contacting us.</p></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "section-3",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n<section class=\"section\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2 id=\"service-quote\">Assessment, work plan and written quote</h2><ol class=\"expanded-steps\"><li><strong>Describe the job.</strong> Give the suburb, affected equipment or planned installation, when it began and whether the condition is worsening. Add safe access and the person who can approve the work.</li><li><strong>Assess the installation.</strong> We check the relevant equipment and connections on site. Concealed work, product compatibility and the cause of a fault cannot be guaranteed from an enquiry or photograph.</li><li><strong>Agree the scope.</strong> The written quote identifies attendance or investigation, the selected equipment, materials and agreed work. Confirm GST, disposal, access, testing and any making good that applies to the specific job.</li><li><strong>Approve changes separately.</strong> If findings change the required work, we explain the additional scope and charge before proceeding. Confirm the checks and completion information needed for a rental or managed property.</li></ol><p>Published standard-hours guide ranges elsewhere on this site are not a fixed price for this unseen job. Emergency repair charges follow the quoted plan. There is no assumed free attendance, unlimited investigation or universal hourly rate.</p></div></section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "service-faq",
"kind": "faq",
"container": "\n<section class=\"section faq\" id=\"service-faq\"><div class=\"shell service-reading\"><h2>24-Hour Emergency Electrician Perth FAQs</h2><!-- site-intent:start --><div class=\"intent-content\" data-site-intent><h3>Prepare the request and approval</h3><p>Give the property location, observable symptoms or intended installation, access contact and the person who can approve the work. The agreed quote sets out the assessment and work; submitting a form does not reserve an appointment.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"electrical.html\">Perth electrical services</a></li><li><a href=\"power-faults-perth.html\">Partial power loss and fault finding</a></li><li><a href=\"safety-switch-tripping-perth.html\">A safety switch that will not reset</a></li><li><a href=\"power-points-perth.html\">Damaged or failed power points</a></li><li><a href=\"contact.html?service=emergency-electrician-perth.html\">Routine electrical enquiries</a></li></ul></div><!-- site-intent:end --><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:0:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:0:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:1:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:1:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:2:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:2:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:3:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:3:answer}}</details></div></section>" as TrustedHtml,
